{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3085","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3085","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3085\",\"parent_revision\":\"77ce0b0f91f8208f057c00ec9758f87dcf6d80ce184f90fafbba92e6f2fb9381\",\"root_revision\":\"77ce0b0f91f8208f057c00ec9758f87dcf6d80ce184f90fafbba92e6f2fb9381\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nNamed as a known gap in ADR-3075-4, not solved there. ADR-3075-4's session-keyed control set\\ndepends on the `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` environment variable being shared between an\\nMCP-tool-calling agent process and any CLI subprocess it spawns in the same session. The only\\nmechanism that populates this variable today is\\n`plugins/development-harness/hooks/session-start-session-id.cjs`, which fires on Claude Code's\\n`SessionStart` hook event and writes the value to `CLAUDE_ENV_FILE` (a Claude-Code-specific\\nmechanism) for later shell commands.\\n\\nThis repo's plugin content targets multiple harnesses (Codex, OpenCode, GitHub's coding agent),\\nnot Claude Code exclusively. Under those harnesses:\\n\\n- There is no `SessionStart` hook event to capture a session ID from.\\n- There is no `CLAUDE_ENV_FILE` mechanism to inject it into subsequent shell commands.\\n- An already-running MCP server has no path to receive the ID either \u2014 the hook only ever\\n  targets the CLI-subprocess side.\\n\\nIn those environments the CLI and MCP paths cannot resolve the same session directory, defeating\\nthe cross-transport guarantee ADR-3075-4 exists to provide (\\\"viewed through one tool, then the\\nCLI, still hits the same entry\\\").\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nBlocked on #3062 (control set must exist first) and ADR-3075-4 (out-of-process, session-keyed\\nstore \u2014 the design this portability gap is specific to).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] A session-ID resolution mechanism exists that supplies the same session key to both the\\n      CLI and MCP paths under at least one non-Claude-Code harness, or\\n- [ ] The session key is passed explicitly through both transports (e.g. as an MCP tool\\n      parameter and a CLI flag/env var) rather than relying on a harness-specific hook\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"008965cd8ccee80e378c674125a79b79b8ea1f6673f2d2146702093dce6c2207\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQIphVg\"}"}